        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat(durable): hand off wakes to session queue",
        "body": "# PR5/5 - internal session delivery handoff + final hardening\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nThis finishes the beta3 durable-core stack by turning resolved durable wake\nobligations into an internal session delivery-queue handoff on gateway startup.\nAfter PR4 made wakes inspectable and controllable, PR5 gives the durable runtime\na concrete recovery path: a resolved wake is replayed, persisted with delivery\nevidence, and queued for the owning OpenClaw session without inventing external\nchannel sends.\n\n## Stack position\n\n- Stack item: PR5/5\n- Clean PR5 comparison: `a30e2b6ce4e5f1390599380aedc82078c98854f7..443ffd2292e146fad3c089a03382a5f4702632f7`\n- PR4 dependency: `https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/105844`\n- GitHub base rationale: existing PR1-PR4 stack PRs target `release/2026.7.1`; the PR4 branch exists on the fork, not as an upstream base branch, so this PR follows stack convention while documenting the exact PR4-head diff.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Adds `createDurableWakeSessionDeliveryHook`, which resolves durable wakes to\n  agent/session keys and enqueues one internal `systemEvent` via the session\n  delivery queue.\n- Wires gateway startup durable wake replay through that hook.\n- Persists delivery evidence with `internalDelivery: \"session_delivery_queue\"`\n  and `noExternalSend: true`.\n- Extends focused replay/startup tests for idempotency, startup replay, ambiguous\n  target handling, and no autonomous resume/abandon/create-new policy.\n- Updates durable docs to clarify the `delivered` state and CLI wake-attempt\n  evidence.\n\n## Non-scope\n\n- No Discord, Signal, Slack, plugin, or other external transport delivery is\n  implemented or claimed.\n- No cron mutation.\n- No release/changelog/package churn from the stale old PR5 ancestry.\n- No broad durable orchestration policy changes beyond this internal handoff.\n\n## Evidence\n\nClean scope:\n\n```text\n6 files changed, 372 insertions(+), 50 deletions(-)\n```\n\nFocused behavior:\n\n```bash\nnode scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/durable/wake-delivery-replay.test.ts src/durable/startup.test.ts\n# pass: 2 files, 14 tests\n```\n\nAdjacent durable CLI/Gateway/read-path proof:\n\n```bash\nnode scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/commands/durable.test.ts src/gateway/server-methods/durable.test.ts src/durable/wake-controls-inspection.test.ts\n# pass: 3 Vitest shards, 4 files, 25 tests\n```\n\nStatic/docs gates:\n\n```bash\npnpm check:test-types\n# pass\n\npnpm check:docs\n# pass\n\ngit diff --check a30e2b6ce4e5f1390599380aedc82078c98854f7..HEAD\n# pass\n```\n\nRemote proof attempts were made but unavailable in this shell:\n\n```text\nblacksmith-testbox: blocked, blacksmith CLI not found in PATH\naws Crabbox: blocked, broker login missing\n```\n\n## Upgrade contract\n\nThis PR adds no schema migration. It writes wake delivery attempts using the\nexisting durable wake attempt ledger and queues internal session deliveries using\nthe existing session delivery queue idempotency contract. Repeated startup replay\nmust not duplicate queued events once a wake is marked delivered.\n\n## Risk / limits\n\n- Main risk is semantic: reviewers should confirm `delivered` remains scoped to\n  internal durable/session handoff and cannot be mistaken for external channel\n  transport success.\n- Remote Testbox proof is still desirable before merge because local provider\n  setup blocked it here.\n- Full release validation was not run for this narrow PR5 slice.\n\n@clawsweeper review\n\n\n\n### Live Gateway startup/restart proof at PR5 head\n\nAdditional live Gateway startup/restart proof at PR5 head `443ffd2292e146fad3c089a03382a5f4702632f7` was collected using a real local Gateway process twice against the same isolated state dir.\n\nThis proof intentionally disables external channels/plugins and does not claim Discord, Slack, Telegram, plugin, or other external transport delivery, end-user-visible consumption, live attached-session consumption, topology cleanup, or merge readiness. In PR5, `delivered` means internal durable/session-queue handoff only: ownership transferred to the persisted session delivery queue.\n\nResult summary:\n\n```text\nstartup 1:\n- real Gateway process started and recorded durable gateway startup\n- one resolved wake moved pending -> delivered\n- exactly-once internal session delivery queue handoff\n- wake delivery attempt count: 1\n- evidence.kind: wake_internal_session_delivery_enqueued\n- evidence.internalDelivery: session_delivery_queue\n- evidence.noExternalSend: true\n- evidence.queueId: dfb326421eea3baa89c510ea5642d11110fc439000a979c32fe1c1b5a9fbba59\n- evidence.sessionKey: agent:main:main\n- pending session delivery count: 1\n- pending queue entry kind: systemEvent\n\nstartup 2 against the same isolated state dir:\n- real Gateway process started again and recorded durable gateway startup\n- wake delivery attempt count remained 1\n- pending session delivery count remained 1\n- queue id remained dfb326421eea3baa89c510ea5642d11110fc439000a979c32fe1c1b5a9fbba59\n- no duplicate wake attempt or queue entry was created\n\nrepo session-delivery recovery API on the same state dir, because no attached local session lifecycle was available:\n- recovered: 1\n- failed: 0\n- skippedMaxRetries: 0\n- deferredBackoff: 0\n- pending session delivery count: 0\n- final wake count: 1\n- final wake delivery attempt count: 1\n```\n\nThe live Gateway startup command used for both starts:\n\n```bash\nenv OPENCLAW_STATE_DIR=\"$STATE_DIR\" \\\n  OPENCLAW_CONFIG_PATH=\"$CONFIG_PATH\" \\\n  OPENCLAW_DURABLE_RUNTIME=1 \\\n  OPENCLAW_DURABLE_WORKER=0 \\\n  OPENCLAW_SKIP_CHANNELS=1 \\\n  OPENCLAW_DISABLE_BUNDLED_PLUGINS=1 \\\n  OPENCLAW_GATEWAY_STARTUP_TRACE=1 \\\n  OPENCLAW_ACPX_RUNTIME_STARTUP_PROBE=0 \\\n  OPENCLAW_DISABLE_PLUGIN_REGISTRY_MIGRATION=1 \\\n  node --import tsx src/entry.ts gateway \\\n    --port \"$PORT\" --bind loopback --auth none --tailscale off \\\n    --allow-unconfigured --ws-log compact --verbose\n```\n\nRepresentative startup logs:\n\n```text\n2026-07-14T00:07:46.606+07:00 [gateway] http server listening (0 plugins, 0.5s)\n2026-07-14T00:07:46.765+07:00 [durable/runtimes] recorded durable gateway startup\n2026-07-14T00:07:47.950+07:00 [shutdown] completed cleanly in 22ms\n\n2026-07-14T00:07:54.070+07:00 [gateway] http server listening (0 plugins, 0.5s)\n2026-07-14T00:07:54.146+07:00 [durable/runtimes] recorded durable gateway startup\n2026-07-14T00:07:55.148+07:00 [shutdown] completed cleanly in 19ms\n```\n\nQueue recovery output:\n\n```text\n[queue-recovery info] Recovered session delivery dfb326421eea3baa89c510ea5642d11110fc439000a979c32fe1c1b5a9fbba59\n```\n\nReset-boundary proof remains scoped to the existing focused test: queued `agentTurn` entries carry `expectedSessionId` and are skipped across a session-generation mismatch, while PR5 durable wake handoff queues a `systemEvent` against the canonical current session key. This surfaces the durable wake internally without autonomous resume or new-session policy.\n\n```bash\nnode scripts/run-vitest.mjs run --config test/vitest/vitest.gateway.config.ts src/gateway/server-restart-sentinel.test.ts -t \"does not dispatch a queued agentTurn continuation after the session key changes|still delivers systemEvent continuations for completed run entries\" --reporter verbose\n# Test Files  1 passed (1)\n# Tests  2 passed | 26 skipped (28)\n```\n\nThe stack topology / CI drift item is unchanged by this proof. The clean PR5 slice does not modify `.github/workflows/ci.yml`, but the public cumulative PR diff still includes workflow drift because the branch is stacked on earlier durable work. That remains a sequencing/rebase issue before merge.\n",
